abstract: >-
  Evolution by Emergence is an open research corpus and machine-auditable
  candidate architecture for resource-constrained cumulative evolution.
  Version v22.7 keeps everything in v22.6: CORE.md follows one model of
  learning, read as a network, in eight steps, and formalization/ebe-
  core/EbECore.lean audits 91 machine-checked results. It adds two pieces of
  writing and no new Lean. An essay, Building the future, states an
  orientation: when answers become cheap, the bottleneck moves from finding
  solutions to taking them up, yesterday's aims become today's tools, and
  prediction becomes a tool to change what it predicts; it is marked as a
  stance, not a result. A concept note, The integrity of world models,
  separates honest error from deliberate manipulation, treats deliberate
  deception and neural intervention as two routes to one harm, reads the five
  neurorights against existing human rights and the relational duties, adds
  the integrity of shared world models as a row they lack, and grounds the
  whole in autonomous interdependence. Retained from earlier releases:
  identity as a learned path with the LearnedIdentity module, TamedCapture,
  duties to the quality of a relationship, a shared identity as learners, and
  a separate section on transparent pricing with its own 76-result core-Lean
  package. DIALOGUE.md records how the author and an AI assistant build the
  model together, now in 33 entries. The release title uses "simulation of
  reality" to mean the internal model through which a system experiences and
  acts in the world, not a claim that reality itself is simulated. Formal
  verification establishes implications under explicit premises; empirical,
  causal, political and normative interpretations remain open.
